<% content_for :title, 'Planetoid Belt' %>

<%= render 'help/page', title: 'Planetoid Belt' do %>
  <div class='space-y-6'>
    <div class='space-y-3 text-fg'>
      <p>
        Displays the survey record for a planetoid belt. Data is organised into
        tabs corresponding to each digit of the Universal World Profile, plus
        supplementary tabs for orbital mechanics and the significant body catalogue.
        The Physical tab presents belt-specific data in place of the standard
        planetary physical fields.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class='font-semibold text-highlight mb-2'>Controls</p>
      <dl class='space-y-5'>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Regenerate</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Submits the belt's Universal World Profile and orbital parameters to the
            generator data core, which recomputes and returns a complete characteristic
            profile. All existing survey data for the belt is superseded by the returned
            values, including the significant body catalogue — all previously recorded
            planetoids are expunged and reconstructed from the generator's output.
            This operation is irreversible. Available only when the belt orbits a stellar
            primary.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class='font-semibold text-highlight mb-2'>Tabs</p>
      <dl class='space-y-5'>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Orbital</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Orbital radius (orbit number and/or AU), period, effective HZCO deviation,
            retrograde flag, inclination, eccentricity, periapsis/apoapsis, and the
            location hierarchy through to sector.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Starport</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Starport classification (A–E, X), allegiance, and travel zone.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Physical</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Belt-specific data: resource rating, bulk, and span. Belt composition is
            expressed as percentage split across metallic (M), stony (S), carbonaceous
            (C), and other (O) material types; these values must total 100%.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Atmo</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Atmosphere code, relevant for belts with trace or exotic gas envelopes.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Hydro</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Hydrographics code, liquid type, and distribution.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Pop</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Population code with headcount range, concentration rating, urbanisation
            percentage, major city count, and cultural indices.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Gov</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Government type, authority, centralisation, and governmental structure. Not shown when population and this value are both 0.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Law</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Law level code with sub-ratings covering restrictions and judicial system. Not shown when population and this value are both 0.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Tech</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>Overall technology level code with per-category sub-ratings. Not shown when population and this value are both 0.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Bodies</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Paginated list of significant bodies within the belt. The tab counter shows
            the total body count. Toggle
            <span class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Significant only</span>
            to suppress sub-kilometre fragments.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class='pt-2 text-right uppercase font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.22em] text-fg-muted'>
      REFERENCE 0626PB
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>